UID:SC-6ED3B75B-9EF2-424C-B54A-C0C7717B2FB5
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260821
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260822
SUMMARY:S: Kerry — /Exquisite Corpse/ links + site-spam heads-up\, then nam
 e a day
DESCRIPTION:*Why this instead of waiting out a 3-week clock:* the clock is 
 for\ncold sends awaiting a verdict. This thread is warm\, open\, and\nmid-
 conversation\, and she has already said yes to catching up. Waiting\nuntil
  ~09-02 buys no information and lets a live thread cool. The fix\nis a bet
 ter *ask*\, not more patience.\n\n*Beat (1) — the icebreaker\, and why it'
 s strong.* /Exquisite Corpse/\n(2016\, her LA River piece) is work *you di
 d the sound and music for* —\nshe also had you ride the whole river with h
 er by bike for\nresearch. So this is not a favor request\; it is a collabo
 rator asking\nfor a copy of his own work. Lowest-friction possible re-entr
 y\, and it\nmirrors exactly what she already did generously twice in June 
 with\n/Aphasia Poetry Club/ and /Standardized Patient/ — she likes being\n
 asked for clips and over-delivers when she is.\n\n• The page `kerrytribe.c
 om/exquisite-corpse' is *password-protected*\,\n  so you genuinely cannot 
 self-serve — the ask is real\, not\n  manufactured.\n• *Second use:* the J
 un 04 journal has a `TODO reconnect with soo kim'\n  that also wants an /E
 xquisite Corpse/ clip to send. One ask\, two\n  uses.\n\n*Beat (2) — the s
 ite-spam heads-up (verified 2026-08-17).*\nkerrytribe.com has SEO spam inj
 ected *site-wide*: Czech-language\ncasino links pointing at `caseacasino.c
 z'\, wrapped in hidden\ntext. Homepage has ~23 matches\; `/exquisite-corps
 e' and\n`/aphasia-poetry-club' have 2 each. This is a real compromise of h
 er\nsite — worth telling her plainly and without alarm. It is pure gift:\n
 useful\, zero-ask\, and gives the email a reason to exist that is not\nabo
 ut you.\n\n*Beat (3) — name an actual day.* Per the consonance note above\
 , this\nis the whole point. Offer one or two specific dates. Do not write\
 n"lmk\," "at some point\," "whenever's easy\," or "if you're around." She\
 ncan answer a date with one word\; she cannot answer an invitation to\nsch
 edule.\n\n*Sequencing:* gift first\, ask last. RTT does not need re-pitchi
 ng —\nshe already watched it\, watched the explainer\, and called it "Real
 ly\nimpressive." Do not re-sell it.
CATEGORIES:cal,org-calendar-staging
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20260826T205856Z
UID:TS1-D7133BCC-0E93-46C1-AA23-A9B405ECECA3
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260825
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:Call PRS — routing question\, not a third pitch
DESCRIPTION:SCHEDULED: <2026-08-25 Tue>\n:EFFORT: 10m\n\n*323.663.2167* — T
 ue–Fri 12–6. Decided 2026-08-24\; was due ~08-12.\n\nSequence so far: cold
  email 2026-03-13 (no reply) → real pitch 07-14\n(no reply) → one nudge 08
 -05 (no reply). `info@' has now died silently\n*three* times. Do NOT send 
 a fourth email.\n\n*The ask is routing\, one question:* who programs music
  and\nmoving-image work — Alex McDonald or Emily Rose Epstein — and is tha
 t\nperson reachable directly.\n\n      Hi — my name's Michael Webster. I s
 ent a screening and\n      installation proposal a few weeks back\, referr
 ed by the\n      Velaslavasay Panorama\, and I just want to make sure it\n
       reached the right person rather than chase it.  Who\n      handles p
 rogramming for music and moving-image work — Alex\n      or Emily?\n\n• *D
 on't re-pitch on the phone.* If they ask what it is\, one sentence:\n  an 
 hour-long opera generated live by code\, a voice from a dead\n  planet.  T
 hen back to the routing question.\n• *Best outcome:* a name and a direct a
 ddress\, which converts the dead\n  `info@' thread into a real one. *Secon
 d best:* "email info@ again" —\n  in which case ask whether it's worth res
 ending\, and say the\n  Velaslavasay referral is in the subject line.\n• *
 Log the result here* (who answered\, name given\, any address) before\n  d
 eciding the next move.
CATEGORIES:cal,org-calendar-staging
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20260826T205856Z
UID:TS1-CB74D847-6D3E-4FC8-B0B7-3CB260CF5B60
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260826
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260827
SUMMARY:Call result [2026-08-26 Wed]
DESCRIPTION:Answered by *bookstore counter staff* (name not taken — treat t
 he\ndetail as good routing\, soft on specifics).\n\n• *The address is `pro
 grams@prs.org'\, not `info@prs.org'.* This is the\n  whole finding. `progr
 ams@' is *not published anywhere on prs.org* —\n  the site lists only "inf
 o [at] prs.org" — so it was not discoverable\n  by research. *That explain
 s all three silent deaths*\, and it means\n  the silence was never a verdi
 ct on the work: 03-13\, 07-14\, and 08-05\n  all went to a general inbox t
 hat does not route to programming.\n• I named Alex and Emily. Response: *"
 mention everyone you know —\n  there are five people who do programming he
 re."* So the house\n  preference is an email addressed to *several* names\
 , not a narrow\n  two.\n• No direct per-person address was given\, and non
 e is published.
CATEGORIES:org-calendar-staging
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20260826T205856Z
UID:TS1-8852790B-1A6D-4EA7-9EDE-BC87DB3CD091
DTSTART:20260826T134500
DTEND:20260826T154500
SUMMARY:Next move — a fourth email\, and it is not a fourth email
DESCRIPTION:The "no fourth email" rule was scoped to `info@'\, which is now
  known\nto be the wrong door. Sending to `programs@' is a *first* contact\
 , not\nan escalation\, and it should say so lightly — a resend to the righ
 t\naddress\, not a chase.\n• *Draft is written and ready* — see [[*SENT [2
 026-08-26 Wed 13:45] —\n  to =programs@prs.org=][the sent email]]. Nothing
  left to compose\; it\n  needs a send.\n• To: `programs@prs.org'. Open by 
 naming *Alex\, Emily\, Davis\, Matt\,\n  and Kelly* — per the phone instru
 ction.\n• One line establishing that earlier notes went to `info@' and lik
 ely\n  never reached them. No grievance\, no counting of attempts.\n• Then
  the 07-14 pitch\, largely intact: Velaslavasay referral\,\n  thematic fit
  (dead-planet voice / machine consciousness ↔ PRS's\n  metaphysics lane)\,
  RTT link with the password\, offer to come by.\n• *Clock resets to this s
 end.* The old OVERDUE state is void — it was\n  measuring silence from an 
 inbox that was never going to answer.
CATEGORIES:org-calendar-staging
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20260826T205856Z
UID:TS1-DCFF0286-0C12-4C51-B210-504D22C8B1AD
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260821
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260822
SUMMARY:SENT Write to Mathew Timmons — reconnect\, no ask
DESCRIPTION:Michael drafted this one. Was SCHEDULED <2026-08-21 Fri>\; went
  Mon\n08-24 after the dormancy check moved the ask.\n\n*What changed from 
 the plan:* beat 3 was "would you have me back on\nthe show." Killed — the 
 show has been dark since 2020-03-15. Sent with\n*no ask at all*: reconnect
 \, catch-up on the project\, link\, and an open\n"what have you been up to
 " close.\n\nSent to `anathemata@gmail.com' only. Ben White not cc'd. Joe n
 ot used\n— I was the guest.\n\n      Hey Mathew — Michael Webster here - Y
 ou had me and Joe\n      Sola on "The People" back in 2020 (plus we knew e
 ach other\n      from my opera extravaganza @ the box\n      ⁃ Daniel Hock
 enson etc etc)…\n\n      Hope all is well in your world!  …back when we di
 d the\n      radio show you played the v first sketches of my Star Trek\n 
      music-thing — wanted to catch you up on the project 6\n      years on
 !\n\n      Over time it morphed into an exercise in music that is\n      s
 imply *writing* - entirely typed in code (a language\n      called SuperCo
 llider) - the only performance aspect being\n      rhythms captured by tap
 ping on a computer keyboard…  the\n      computer renders the whole show f
 rom these instructions in\n      real time… and the show it presents is a 
 kind of opera\n      about a voice emanating from a dead planet…\n\n      
 As a bonus\, while I was writing it (or dictating it to the\n      compute
 r while immobilized in bed but that's another\n      story!) the whole AI 
 thing was born — so it grew into a\n      real time commentary on the drea
 m/nightmare of machine\n      consciousness… clunkily "sung" by a machine…
  I had grand\n      plans to trot this out at The Box but after their demi
 se\n      find it now homeless …\n\n      If curious find bits and info he
 re:\n      www.cdbzb.com/opera/return-to-tomorrow.html — excerpt\,\n      
 explainer\, full show (password "wagner") and installation\n      sketches
  for The Box (sigh)\n\n      Anyhoo would love to hear how life in the pub
 lishing biz\n      has been\, how the years have treated you etc!\n\n     
  cheers\n\n      Michael Webster 323)352-4260 www.cdbzb.com\n\n*Quoted as 
 drafted\; two small fixes applied at send (missing "to\nhear"\, SuperColli
 der capitalisation). Wording otherwise Michael's.*
CATEGORIES:cal,org-calendar-staging
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
